{"id": "logic_020", "category": "logic", "mode": "council", "question": "If it takes 5 machines 5 minutes to make 5 widgets, how many minutes would it take 100 machines to make 100 widgets?", "answer": "To determine how long it would take 100 machines to make 100 widgets, we need to understand the relationship between the number of machines, the number of widgets, and the time it takes to produce them.\n\nFirst, let's establish the rate at which the machines produce widgets. If 5 machines take 5 minutes to produce 5 widgets, then the rate of production is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Rate} = \\frac{5 \\text{ widgets}}{5 \\text{ machines} \\times 5 \\text{ minutes}} = \\frac{1 \\text{ widget}}{5 \\text{ minutes}} \\]\n\nThis means that each machine produces 1 widget in 5 minutes.\n\nNow, we need to find out how long it would take 100 machines to produce 100 widgets. Since each machine produces 1 widget in 5 minutes, 100 machines would produce 100 widgets in:\n\n\\[ \\text{Time} = 100 \\text{ machines} \\times 5 \\text{ minutes per machine} = 500 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nTherefore, it would take 100 machines 500 minutes to make 100 widgets.", "speaker": "qwen2.5-0.5b-worker", "correct": true, "score_method": "contains", "gold": "5", "elapsed_s": 8.7, "rss_gb": 7.71, "meta": {"rounds_trace": [{"round": 1, "agreement": 0.7575, "unanimous": true, "top1": "that", "entropy": 0.0, "opinions": [{"name": "Commander", "entropy": 2.48, "top": [["that", 0.574], ["not", 0.17], ["given", 0.073], ["the", 0.05]], "vec_idx": 4786}, {"name": "Scout-A", "entropy": 8.54, "top": [["that", 0.145], ["not", 0.069], ["given", 0.041], ["the", 0.032]], "vec_idx": 4787}, {"name": "Scout-B", "entropy": 8.39, "top": [["that", 0.157], ["not", 0.072], ["given", 0.043], ["the", 0.033]], "vec_idx": 4788}, {"name": "Worker-1", "entropy": 2.65, "top": [["that", 0.535], ["not", 0.186], ["given", 0.08], ["the", 0.047]], "vec_idx": 4789}, {"name": "Worker-2", "entropy": 2.41, "top": [["that", 0.566], ["not", 0.19], ["gi